PCT_planner contains several third party libraries, with documentation of licensing
and modifications as follows:

- gtsam 4.1.1: Georgia Tech Smoothing and Mapping Library
        - Local changes are limited to the exact BSD-3-Clause identifier in
            package.xml and wrap/setup.py.
        - Licensed under BSD-3-Clause; see
            planner/lib/3rdparty/gtsam-4.1.1/LICENSE.BSD.
- osqp 0.6.2: The Operator Splitting QP Solver
        - The local snapshot adds include/osqp_configure.h and
            lin_sys/direct/qdldl/qdldl_sources/include/qdldl_types.h for the retained
            offline/aarch64 build configuration; no upstream file is modified.
        - Licensed under Apache-2.0; see planner/lib/3rdparty/osqp/LICENSE and NOTICE.
- pybind11 2.11.0.dev1: Seamless operability between C++11 and Python
        - The retained files are byte-identical to the recorded PCT baseline.
        - License text is in planner/lib/3rdparty/pybind11/LICENSE.
- Eigen embedded by GTSAM
        - The retained files are byte-identical to the recorded PCT baseline.
        - Eigen's COPYING.README says the tree is primarily MPL-2.0 while some
            files use BSD or LGPL terms. Preserve the complete COPYING.* set; this
            project does not claim that every embedded Eigen file is MPL-2.0-only.

